{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5192) from a code generation pipeline. The task is to create differential tests for `cmd/hostid` implementing SRD requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3 from `srd048-hostid`. Specifically, create `cmd/hostid/hostid_test.go` that compares the Go hostid binary against the GNU reference binary `ghostid` using the project's `pkg/testutils` differential testing framework.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: running Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, comparing stdout, stderr, and exit codes\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.BuildBinary` for test infrastructure\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"ghostid\")` for finding the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n   - `t.Skip` for graceful degradation when reference binary is missing\n   - LC_ALL=C environment setting (handled automatically by testutils.buildEnv)\n   - SRD048-hostid requirements R3.1-R3.3 (differential test requirements)\n   - The hostid utility prints a 32-bit host identifier as 8-digit lowercase hex\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd048-hostid.yaml`\n     - Read to understand the requirements R3.1-R3.3\n     - R3.1: Tests must compare stdout and exit codes via pkg/testutils\n     - R3.2: Must cover: normal invocation (no args), extra operand error, unknown flag error\n     - R3.3: All tests must set LC_ALL=C\n   \n   - `cmd/hostid/main.go` (existing, 68 lines)\n     - Read to understand the implementation being tested\n     - Prints 8-digit hex from `syscall.SysctlUint32(\"kern.hostid\")`\n     - Handles --help, --version, rejects unknown flags (exit 1), rejects extra operands (exit 1)\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd048-hostid R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: hostid [OPTION]\n     Print the numeric identifier (as a hexadecimal number) for the current host.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     const versionText = `hostid (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         for len(args) > 0 {\n             switch args[0] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--\":\n                 args = args[1:]\n                 goto done\n             default:\n                 if strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n                     fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 goto done\n             }\n         }\n     done:\n         if len(args) > 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         hostid, err := syscall.SysctlUint32(\"kern.hostid\")\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: %v\\n\", err)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%08x\\n\", hostid); err != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided inline in project_context)\n     - Contains DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests function, buildEnv (sets LC_ALL=C by default)\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest{Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles}`, `RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`, `BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n\n   - `cmd/hostid/hostid_test.go` - TO BE CREATED\n     - Must follow the differential testing pattern\n     - Must test: no-args invocation, extra operand error (exit 1), unknown flag error (exit 1)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD and existing implementation to understand the test cases needed\n   - No problems encountered yet as implementation hasn't started\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. The task is to create differential tests for cmd/hostid implementing srd048-hostid R3.1-R3.3.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Request for a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/hostid/hostid_test.go` with differential tests covering:\n     - Normal invocation (no arguments) - should match ghostid output\n     - Extra operand error (e.g., `hostid extraarg`) - exit code 1\n     - Unknown flag error (e.g., `hostid --unknown`) - exit code 1\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/hostid/` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/hostid/... -count=1` to verify tests compile and pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two requir