{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3jmPZJ828Q7LRLn4hKC8h","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found the `DiffTest.Normalize` field definition and several examples of how tests use it to normalize stderr and stdout for comparisons between Go and reference binaries.\n\n### DiffTest.Normalize Definition\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 44-53):\n\nThe `Normalize` field is defined as:\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string\n    Args          []string\n    Stdin         []byte\n    Env           []string\n    WorkDir       string\n    ExitCode      int\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc        // <-- This field\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n\n// NormalizeFunc is a type alias for normalization functions\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\nThe `Normalize` field holds a slice of `NormalizeFunc` functions that are applied in order to both stdout and stderr of both binaries before comparison (lines 168-173):\n\n```go\nfunc applyNormalizers(res binaryResult, fns []NormalizeFunc) binaryResult {\n    for _, fn := range fns {\n        res.stdout = fn(res.stdout)\n        res.stderr = fn(res.stderr)\n    }\n    return res\n}\n```\n\n### Example 1: `basename` - Binary Name Normalization\n\nFile: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/cmd/basename/basename_test.go` (lines 23-26)\n\nThis example handles program name differences between the Go binary and GNU reference:\n\n```go\nbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`)\nnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"basename\"))\n})\n```\n\nThen used in error test cases (lines 107-116):\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"error-no-args\",\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n{\n    Name:      \"error-extra-operand\",\n    Args:      []string{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n```\n\nThis regex matches paths like `/path/to/basename` or `/path/to/gbasename` and replaces them with just `basename`, normalizing stderr messages that include the program name.\n\n### Example 2: `head` - Discarding Stderr\n\nFile: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/cmd/head/head_test.go` (lines 23-24, 147-148)\n\nThis example simply discards stderr to handle error message differences:\n\n```go\ndiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n```\n\nUsed when error messages differ between implementations (line 147):\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"bytes-invalid\",\n    Args:      []string{\"-c\", \"abc\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n},\n```\n\nAlso used for file-not-found error cases (lines 244, 252, 260, 268) where stderr would contain absolute file paths that differ between binaries.\n\n### Key Points\n\n1. **Program name handling**: Regex-based normalization strips program path prefixes and the `g` prefix from GNU binary names to handle stderr messages that reference the program name.\n\n2. **Selective discarding**: When error messages are too different to normalize, the entire output stream (stderr or stdout) can be discarded by returning `nil`.\n\n3. **Multiple normalizers**: The `Normalize` field accepts a slice, allowing multiple normalization functions to be chained together via `ComposeNormalizers` if needed.\n\n4. **Scope**: Normalizers apply to **both** stdout and stderr of **both** binaries before comparison, ensuring fair comparison despite implementation differences."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8fadd41-3dca-4446-bafd-ef6a12644cab","uuid":"db76656f-c89f-4b9b-a353-6d11392a5363","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:21:10.419Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192, search cmd/ directories for test files that use `Normalize` in DiffTest definitions. I need to see how they normalize stderr to handle program name differences between Go and reference binaries. Show me a couple of examples with context. Also check how the DiffTest.Normalize field is defined in pkg/testutils/difftest.go.","agentId":"a4618ea4677465eee","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary\n\nI found the `DiffTest.Normalize` field definition and several examples of how tests use it to normalize stderr and stdout for comparisons between Go and reference binaries.\n\n### DiffTest.Normalize Definition\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 44-53):\n\nThe `Normalize` field is defined as:\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string\n    Args          []string\n    Stdin         []byte\n    Env           []string\n    WorkDir       string\n    ExitCode      int\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc        // <-- This field\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n\n// NormalizeFunc is a type alias for normalization functions\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\n\nThe `Normalize` field holds a slice of `NormalizeFunc` functions that are applied in order to both stdout and stderr of both binaries before comparison (lines 168-173):\n\n```go\nfunc applyNormalizers(res binaryResult, fns []NormalizeFunc) binaryResult {\n    for _, fn := range fns {\n        res.stdout = fn(res.stdout)\n        res.stderr = fn(res.stderr)\n    }\n    return res\n}\n```\n\n### Example 1: `basename` - Binary Name Normalization\n\nFile: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/cmd/basename/basename_test.go` (lines 23-26)\n\nThis example handles program name differences between the Go binary and GNU reference:\n\n```go\nbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?basename`)\nnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n    return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"basename\"))\n})\n```\n\nThen used in error test cases (lines 107-116):\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"error-no-args\",\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n{\n    Name:      \"error-extra-operand\",\n    Args:      []string{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n},\n```\n\nThis regex matches paths like `/path/to/basename` or `/path/to/gbasename` and replaces them with just `basename`, normalizing stderr messages that include the program name.\n\n### Example 2: `head` - Discarding Stderr\n\nFile: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5192/cmd/head/head_test.go` (lines 23-24, 147-148)\n\nThis example simply discards stderr to handle error message differences:\n\n```go\ndiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n```\n\nUsed when error messages differ between implementations (line 147):\n```go\n{\n    Name:      \"bytes-invalid\",\n    Args:      []string{\"-c\", \"abc\"},\n    ExitCode:  1,\n    Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n},\n```\n\nAlso used for file-not-found error cases (lines 244, 252, 260, 268) where stderr would contain absolute file paths that differ between binaries.\n\n### Key Points\n\n1. **Program name handling**: Regex-based normalization strips program path prefixes and the `g` prefix from GNU binary names to handle stderr messages that reference the program name.\n\n2. **Selective discarding**: When error messages are too different to normalize, the entire output stream (stderr or stdout) can be discarded by returning `nil`.\n\n3. **Multiple normalizers**: The `Normalize` field accepts a slice, allowing multiple normalization functions to be chained together via `ComposeNormalizers` if needed.\n\n4. **Scope**: Normalizers apply to **both** stdout and stderr of **both** binaries before comparison, ensuring fair comparison despite implementation differences."}],"totalDurationMs":21935,"totalTokens":29877,"totalToolUseCount":8,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5591,"cache_read_input_tokens":23183,"output_tokens":1098,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5591},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":1098,"cache_read_input_tokens":23183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5591,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":4,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
